### Q20 — Topic 3.7 *(select TWO)*

A CI pipeline lets an agent run cloud and database CLIs to diagnose failed deployments.
Today it is unrestricted and uses a senior developer’s admin credentials exported into CI.
The team wants to keep the CLI approach. Which TWO controls most reduce the risk?

A) Convert every CLI to an MCP server before allowing any agent use.

B) Instruct the agent in CLAUDE.md to avoid destructive commands.

C) Enforce a permission allowlist of specific commands and subcommands, explicitly denying
   destructive ones.

D) Run the CLIs with credentials scoped to what the CI job needs, not a developer’s admin
   credentials.

E) Log every command and review the log monthly.

